/P 313 0 R
/E (Even in these designs, triangles appear implicitly. Consider a stone arch: while the stones are curved, the force vectors \(the paths the weight takes to reach the ground\) don't follow the curve perfectly. Instead, the compression forces resolve into a series of straight lines. If you were to map these internal stresses, you would see a "polygonal" chain. The arch remains stable because these force paths form a network of virtual triangles that lock the structure in place.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
