/E (Another method often used to prevent bread from going stale is the use of fats, such as butter, olive oil or animal fat in the production of bread. Because fats are mostly apolar and, as such, hydrophobic \(they repel water\), the addition of fats helps to slow the migration of water during the recrystallisation process, keeping the crumb moist.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [5]
>>
