677 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 335 0 R
/E (For decades, scientists had an answer, and it wasn't a flattering one; they called it junk. Not a technical term - just an honest shrug. These were sequences that didn't seem to serve any useful purpose: leftovers from millions of years of evolution, accumulated without purpose. It was a reasonable conclusion given what was known at the time. What followed was a gradual, and still unfinished, realisation that the picture was far more complicated.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [5]
>>
